<title>CANADA: Canada approves CWB C$25/T durum wheat price rise.</title>
<headline>Canada approves CWB C$25/T durum wheat price rise.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada approved Thursday a C$25/tonne rise in an initial downpayment it guarantees on durum wheat grown by some of the Canadian Wheat Board's 115,369 farmers in crop year 1996/97 (Aug/July), according to a CWB statement.</p>
<p>The C$25 a tonne initial payment increase for No1, No2 and No3 Canada Western Amber Durum wheat and a C$10 a tonne rise in price for No4 CWAD takes effect April 28, 1997.</p>
<p>There will be no rise for No5 CWAD, the CWB said.</p>
<p>Adjustment payments will be made to farmers who delivered between August 1, 1996, and April 27, 1997, CWB said.  </p>
